    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0037" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg31"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Pauncefote to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 315.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Newport, R.
                                I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-10-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In pursuance of instructions which I have
                    received from Her Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs, I
                    have the honor to communicate to you the text of an agreement between Great
                    Britain and Germany relating to the present trouble in China, which was signed
                    in London on the 16th instant by the Marquis of Salisbury and the German
                    ambassador on behalf of their respective Governments, and to invite the
                    acceptance by the United States of the principles recorded in that
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d36-a1.xml" xpointer="d36-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
